#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:1
msgid "Build Status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:3
msgid "Run multiple promise-returning & async functions with limited concurrency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:5
msgid "Install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:11
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:31
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:33
msgid "pLimit(concurrency)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:35
msgid "Returns a `limit` function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:37
msgid "concurrency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:39
msgid "Type: `number` Minimum: `1` Default: `Infinity`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:43
msgid "Concurrency limit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:45
msgid "limit(fn, ...args)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:47
msgid "Returns the promise returned by calling `fn(...args)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:49
msgid "fn"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:51
msgid "Type: `Function`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:53
msgid "Promise-returning/async function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:55
msgid "args"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:57
msgid "Any arguments to pass through to `fn`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:59
msgid ""
"Support for passing arguments on to the `fn` is provided in order to be "
"able to avoid creating unnecessary closures. You probably don't need this"
" optimization unless you're pushing a *lot* of functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:61
msgid "limit.activeCount"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:63
msgid "The number of promises that are currently running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:65
msgid "limit.pendingCount"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:67
msgid ""
"The number of promises that are waiting to run (i.e. their internal `fn` "
"was not called yet)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:69
msgid "limit.clearQueue()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:71
msgid "Discard pending promises that are waiting to run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:73
msgid ""
"This might be useful if you want to teardown the queue at the end of your"
" program's lifecycle or discard any function calls referencing an "
"intermediary state of your app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:75
msgid "Note: This does not cancel promises that are already running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:77
msgid "FAQ"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:79
msgid ""
"How is this different from the "
"[`p-queue`](https://github.com/sindresorhus/p-queue) package?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:81
msgid ""
"This package is only about limiting the number of concurrent executions, "
"while `p-queue` is a fully featured queue implementation with lots of "
"different options, introspection, and ability to pause the queue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:83
msgid "Related"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:85
msgid ""
"[p-queue](https://github.com/sindresorhus/p-queue) - Promise queue with "
"concurrency control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:86
msgid ""
"[p-throttle](https://github.com/sindresorhus/p-throttle) - Throttle "
"promise-returning & async functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:87
msgid ""
"[p-debounce](https://github.com/sindresorhus/p-debounce) - Debounce "
"promise-returning & async functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-limit_readme.md:88
msgid ""
"[p-all](https://github.com/sindresorhus/p-all) - Run promise-returning & "
"async functions concurrently with optional limited concurrency"
msgstr ""

